WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.533
It's been

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.768
23 days

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.969
since a train carrying

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.437
hazardous materials

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.772
went off the rails

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.540
in East Palestine, Ohio.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.942
23 days of dread

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:12.212
for the nearly 5000 Americans now asking

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.180
whether their air is safe to breathe

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.282
and their water is safe to drink.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.585
And like so much else in America,

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.919
this environmental disaster

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.654
quickly divided the country

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.089
along partizan lines.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.257
Former President Trump led

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.359
that charge when he visited the town

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.560
inside a deep

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.662
red pocket of Ohio on Wednesday.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.966
Unfortunately, as you know,

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.801
in too many cases, your goodness

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.136
and perseverance,

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.470
you are met with indifference

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.671
and betrayal.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.006
In some cases,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.175
they were doing nothing for you.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.644
They were intending to do

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.380
absolutely nothing for you.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.249
Transportation Secretary Pete Buda, judge

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.683
who visited the town

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.552
a day after Trump's trip,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.721
flatly dismissed that accusation.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.057
What we've seen

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.259
is industry goes to Washington

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.794
and they get their way.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.396
They got their way on a Christmas tree

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.531
of regulatory changes

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.598
that the last administration

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.200
made on his way out the door

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.569
in December of 20, 20

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.738
but caught in the middle of all of this

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.872
are the residents of East

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.641
Palestine who just want to know

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.010
if it's safe to resume their lives.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.112
Just listen to one resident confront

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.447
the CEO of the rail

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.482
company at a CNN town hall last week.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.619
And feel safe in this town now.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.388
You took it away from me.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.556
Did you shorten my life?

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.724
Now I want to retire and enjoy it.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.560
How are we going to enjoy it?

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.128
Do I mow the grass Do I

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.130
can I plant tomatoes next summer?

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.165
What can I do?

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:39.699
Every day

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.235
I cough through a little cough here.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:42.836
A little cough.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.471
I've never had it

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.773
I got rashes on my cheek

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.476
and all my arm from the firm to do.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:50.910
I don't call it a rail

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.847
and I call it a disaster.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.648
Let's discuss all of this

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.750
and more with CNN's Jeff Zeleny,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.452
CNN's Melanie Sloan,

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.386
Politico's Heidi

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.723
Przybyla, and The Atlantic's Adam Harris.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.727
This is become a much bigger situation,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.795
I think, than

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.063
the White House anticipated.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:10.363
They would

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.865
they would concede that,

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.433
but they didn't really see the politics

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.300
of this coming.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.969
But I want to start, though,

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.871
just from a real perspective.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.739
We just heard from that man.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.574
The people of East Palestine are asking

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.243
for really practical things.

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.177
They're asking for water.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.378
They're asking for help.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.779
And if the question is,

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.014
is that being provided

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.282
from the federal government,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.383
here is the answer

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.385
that the Ohio governor has given,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.154
who is a Republican Mike DeWine.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.222
He said, yes, the president called him.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.324
He said, we don't need anything.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.259
Here's his spokesperson

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.593
telling The Washington Post

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.394
that the agencies

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.929
provide the appropriate response

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.264
and was the president of the White House

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:45.899
in touch with the governor frequently?

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.434
The answer to those questions are yes.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.236
He also described the EPA,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.072
the EPA, as extremely responsive

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.942
So on some level,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:56.876
there's the practical

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.710
and there's a political

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.846
from the practical perspective,

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.948
the Republicans in the state say

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.583
the federal government is responding

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.851
But on the political,

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.052
we're hearing something else.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.020
Without question.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.420
You know,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:07.954
and the White House,

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:08.855
if you talk to officials,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.356
they will concede that they were slow

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.392
to recognize the optics

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.793
of the seriousness of this.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.862
They did send the EPA.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.563
And the president

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.631
does not go to every disaster site.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.500
It's not of course it's not possible.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.267
The vice president

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.835
doesn't go to every disaster site.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.370
There weren't any fatalities in this.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.171
So they were

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:25.872
sort of sending

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.840
the appropriate officials

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.908
as they saw them.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.743
There's about a thousand

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:31.544
a train derailments

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.412
every year in the country.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.913
This is different on many levels

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.281
because of the optics of it.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.083
Yes, there are serious

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.418
questions and ramifications

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.353
about the soil, about water.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.588
But really, this became

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.591
seized upon by

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:45.091
the right

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:45.858
wing media

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:49.028
in many respects and fanned the flames.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.063
And the Biden administration

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.231
allowed them to do that

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.633
because they did not optics Leigh Show.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.268
And it was all happening at the same time

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.170
the president was in Ukraine.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.172
So just this confluence of events

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.773
it made, it is Palestine

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.741
versus Ukraine

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.176
and it really just shined a light

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.544
on the divide in the country.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.646
And of course, this county, Columbiana

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.214
County.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:11.584
72% voted for Trump and 27%.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.152
And we had we have those numbers.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.021
And it's an interesting

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.155
the political dynamics here.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.657
I mean, look at this county.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.626
2000. It went for Bush by three.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.493
By 20, 20.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.562
It was up Trump by 40. Five.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.397
So this is absolutely Trump country.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.132
It makes sense that he would be there

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.533
and that he would be pressing the

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.668
peace process.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.336
And it also coincides with him

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.038
launching his campaign

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:32.872
and I might also note

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.806
that this is

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.108
one of those places in the country

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.976
that you would consider a news desert.

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.077
So a lot of these people

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:41.147
who are his supporters don't realize

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.316
that a lot of the policies

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.984
that the Trump administration

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.520
stood for are policies that might

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.088
or stood against,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.157
might, might have helped in this case,

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.059
including gutting the EPA.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.594
The EPA were the first ones out there

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.628
monitoring the water,

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.797
monitoring the toxic fumes,

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.166
the train regulations that were gutted

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.168
under Trump Again,

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.002
these are all things

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.137
that you question yourself.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.538
Would these things have helped?

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.773
And then thirdly,

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:07.874
the tax cuts,

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.142
the corporate tax cuts

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.643
that a lot of these companies

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.544
took advantage

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.745
of were not required

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.280
to be reinvested into things

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.982
like safety regulations.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.216
But these are not things

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.518
that his voters are going to know.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:19.852
So they're very impressionable.

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.721
This is a very emotional issue.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.622
We're not going to know

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.357
for possibly decades

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.625
the full ramifications

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:26.826
of the health impact

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:27.794
on a lot of these resources.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.162
And interestingly,

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.430
the governor, Mike DeWine,

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.031
is saying to Congress,

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.232
this train wasn't marked

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:33.833
as carrying

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.268
extremely hazardous materials,

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.002
and so it wasn't

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.970
subject to a lot of regulations.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:38.738
Why is that?

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.573
Is Congress going to fix that?

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:41.641
But I want to play here.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.142
This is what President Biden said

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.177
to reporters on Friday

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.812
about whether he would go

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:46.746
to East Palestine

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.216
where he planning to travel to.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.285
He called this problem not.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.220
I've spoken with every single major

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.255
figure in both the United Way

00:05:56.289 --> 00:06:00.560
and both Pennsylvania and Ohio.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.629
And so the idea that we're not engaged

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.833
is is simply not not there.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.167
What do you make of that? Adam?

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.168
Should he go?

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:10.770
You know, as Jeff said, right.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.904
This this

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:13.172
president's don't travel

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.640
to every disaster, anything.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.142
The optics of this. Right.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:19.178
He's travel to Ukraine at this point.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.314
It is probably politically smart

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:22.415
for him to travel

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.950
to Palestine, Ohio,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.152
in order to to sort of,

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:27.286
you know, remind people

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.055
that, yes, it's not just my agencies

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:29.322
that are here,

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.357
but it is also to me

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:32.525
that that is here for you as well.

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:33.626
But as you were as you were saying,

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.061
this was a county

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.163
that the president, the former president

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.298
carried by a significant margin. Right.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:40.233
If there's one thing that we know

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.300
about the former president,

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.803
he enjoys shoring up his base.

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:45.905
He likes to talk to his people.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:46.839
And so it's not a surprise

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:47.840
that he went out there.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:48.808
And it's also not a surprise

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.343
that Republicans have seized on something

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.011
where they've talked for years

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:52.412
about this

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:53.045
being a place

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.614
that America's forgotten about.

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:57.150
The Democrats have forgotten about

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.185
that when the president doesn't visit

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.720
a place like East Palestine,

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.221
it becomes a significant issue.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:02.555
Yeah.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:03.956
And I think at this point,

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.758
Jeff, you made this point,

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:06.926
the White House

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:07.960
